[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114539,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "<p>Metastasizing ameloblastoma (MA) is an ameloblastoma that has metastasized despite a benign histopathological appearance in the primary and metastatic foci.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:17:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114540,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9310/3 Ameloblastoma, metastasizing</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114541,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.0 &amp; XH96J9 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of skull or face &amp; Ameloblastoma, metastasizing</p>\r\n<p>2E83.1 &amp; XH96J9 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of lower jaw &amp; Ameloblastoma, metastasizing</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114542,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> benign metastasizing ameloblastoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended</em>: malignant ameloblastoma; malignant adamantinoma; metastatic ameloblastoma; atypical ameloblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114543,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114544,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "<p>The primary tumour develops more frequently in the mandible than in the maxilla {32659412; 33394372}. The most common sites of metastasis are the lungs, followed by the cervical lymph nodes {33394372}, with distant metastasis in approximately 68% of MAs {32659412}. Infrequently reported metastatic sites include bone, brain, liver, and pericardium {15891309; 24152624; 29747056; 30775320; 33394372}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:18:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114545,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Symptoms vary by site; some patients are asymptomatic. Pulmonary metastases may cause dry cough, haemoptysis, and dyspnoea {28944145; 32132332}. Metastasis may be diagnosed concurrently with the primary tumour or after a variable, often long, latent period (range: 0&ndash;45&nbsp;years; mean: 11&nbsp;years) {20970910; 33394372}. Metastases retain the benign ameloblastoma growth pattern.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114546,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Incidence data are only available combined with ameloblastic carcinoma, which is more common; the combined annual cumulative incidence is 1.79&nbsp;cases per 10&nbsp;million person-years {25692490}. MA has a mean age at diagnosis of 45&nbsp;years and a slight male predominance {32659412; 33394372}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114547,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "<p>MA harbours <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutations {25475564}. Risk factors for metastasis include large size, rapid enlargement, protracted clinical course, inadequate removal, and multiple recurrences at the primary site {32659412}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:18:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114548,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Metastasis may result from haematogenous spread during surgical treatment of the primary {32659412}. Alternatively, metastasis could be driven by additional genetic alterations without histopathological changes {32659412}, but no putative molecular markers of metastatic behaviour have been identified {31169204}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114549,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Features are identical to those of conventional ameloblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114550,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MA exhibits identical histopathological features to conventional ameloblastoma, with no specific features predicting metastasis. Among reported MA cases, the plexiform histological pattern is most common {20970910; 33394372}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114551,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "<p>FNAC has been employed in some cases for evaluating metastatic deposits, although cytological features alone are not sufficient for conclusive diagnosis {12804548; 19446199}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-10T12:36:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114552,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114553,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> benign conventional ameloblastoma in the primary tumour and metastasis; no cytological atypia or features of malignancy in the primary tumour or metastasis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114554,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114555,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MA has an overall mean survival time of 5&nbsp;years on systematic review {33394372}. Surgery is the mainstay of treatment; radiotherapy and chemotherapy have no proven benefit {21459020; 32659412}. BRAF-targeted therapy has been reported in limited cases {25475564; 31340860}. Recurrence occurs in about one&nbsp;quarter of cases and is associated with increased mortality {32659412}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:28:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]